      "question": {
        ":question/id": "3e635c06-8620-5bb9-8b31-10b9067044d7",
        ":question/problem": "Which of the following augmented matrices have coefficient matrices that are in row echelon form? Treat the final column of each augmented matrix as its constants column.\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-9 & -9 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -8 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right],\\,B=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 4 & 7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4\\end{array}\\right],\\,C=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-1 & -5 & -2 & -7 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
        ":question/worked-solution": "A coefficient matrix, obtained by omitting the final column of its augmented matrix, is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the bottom of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column to the right of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The coefficient matrix of $A$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-9 & -9 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -8 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The coefficient matrix of $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 4 & 7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The coefficient matrix of $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-1 & -5 & -2 & -7 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ have coefficient matrices that are in row echelon form.",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
