      "question": {
        ":question/id": "6af5e612-ab20-5068-8971-cb405eb7089f",
        ":question/problem": "Which of the following augmented matrices have coefficient matrices that are **not** in row echelon form? Treat the final column of each augmented matrix as its constants column.\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-7 & 1 & -8 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 7\\end{array}\\right],\\,B=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}8 & 8 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -2 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -9 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{array}\\right],\\,C=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}3 & 0 & 3 & -3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 & -7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -9 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 & -2\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
        ":question/worked-solution": "A coefficient matrix, obtained by omitting the final column of its augmented matrix, is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\nI. All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n\nII. Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The coefficient matrix of $A$ is not in row echelon form since ${a}_{33}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-7 & 1 & -8 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 7\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The coefficient matrix of $B$ is not in row echelon form since the second row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nB=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}8 & 8 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -2 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -9 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The coefficient matrix of $C$ is not in row echelon form since ${c}_{33}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nC=\\left[\\begin{array}{cccc|c}3 & 0 & 3 & -3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 & -7 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -9 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2 & -2\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ have coefficient matrices that are **not** in row echelon form.",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
