        ":question/problem": "Which of the following augmented matrices have coefficient matrices that are in row echelon form? Treat the final column of each augmented matrix as its constants column.\n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}5 & 5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -6 & -7 & 7\\end{array}\\right],\\,\\,B=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 9 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 & 8\\end{array}\\right],\\,\\,C=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-4 & -1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -9 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -7\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
        ":question/worked-solution": "A coefficient matrix, obtained by omitting the final column of its augmented matrix, is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the bottom of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column to the right of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The coefficient matrix of $A$ is not in row echelon form since ${a}_{32}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated). \n\n$$\nA=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}5 & 5 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -6 & -7 & 7\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The coefficient matrix of $B$ is not in row echelon form since the first row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nB=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}0 & 0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 9 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 8 & 8\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\n- The coefficient matrix of $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-4 & -1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -9 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -7\\end{array}\\right]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $C$ has a coefficient matrix that is in row echelon form.",
